    "body": "Fixes #271.\n\nKeep repeated `FileCacheLazy.get()` calls consistent with the first read: reuse the cached value and propagate provenance to each recipient without reading or releasing the backing reference again.\n\n## Review changes\n\nRemoved the documentation addition and standalone unit-test file requested by the reviewer. The regression is folded into the existing crude-dataset/cache end-to-end path. No cache eviction, storage format, multiprocessing policy or decoding behavior is changed.\n\n## Current validation\n\nVerified head `cb3b0afbaf84b05145f8310cf56b2969244683c1`. 11 passed, 24 warnings in 9.33s\n\nRefreshed onto current develop. The existing crude-dataset end-to-end tests, cache-pool tests and sample utility tests pass with real files and worker processes on CPU/Python 3.12. Full repository Ruff passes. Native temporary storage was used for Unix IPC sockets because exFAT cannot host those sockets; all source and environment work remains on the contribution volume. \n\nFull repository Ruff passes. The complete all-extras suite, GPU decoding, distributed training and remote-service integration were not run locally. Upstream workflows still require maintainer approval where indicated.\n",
