      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "body": "I don't think this needs documentation in the main docs. This should be taken for granted.",
      "commit_id": "e33a90fc0be336ea486ba150930cabd194a698b5",
      "created_at": "2026-10-07T11:40:22Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -241,6 +241,8 @@ Later, when the packing is computed, we need to retrieve the pixel values.\n In practice, this means the cooker will use a cache pool to queue the data retrieval from an auxiliary data source and obtain a lazy object (a handle to this future data). In a later stage (like {py:meth}`pack_selected_samples <megatron.energon.TaskEncoder.pack_selected_samples>`), the lazy object can be used to retrieve the content.\n Ideally, in the mean-time, the cache pool has already downloaded the data to a local SSD.\n \n+Calling `get(sample)` again on the same lazy reference reuses the loaded value and adds its source information to the supplied sample, without reading or releasing the cache entry a second time.",
